{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:f3472a74bc480a915c2a3875c505fd5b3ebe475d25cefdae9447002ed88b0106", "sample_idx": 32, "model_name": "nvidia/llama-3.3-nemotron-super-49b-v1", "content": "Oregon's pioneering drug decriminalization policy will end on Sunday, replaced by a new law that recriminalizes possession of small amounts of hard drugs. The new law, HB4002, offers individuals caught with illicit substances the option to choose between charges or treatment, including behavioral health programs and deflection initiatives to avoid fines. Possession for personal use will be classified as a misdemeanor, punishable by up to six months in jail.\n\n***\n\nThe primary goal of HB4002 is to facilitate stricter police enforcement of public drug use and impose harsher penalties for selling drugs near specific locations like parks. While the law encourages counties to establish treatment alternatives, diverting individuals from the criminal justice system to addiction and mental health services, it does not make this mandatory. Proponents argue this flexibility allows counties to tailor programs to their resources, whereas opponents foresee a potentially confusing and inequitable policy landscape.\n\n***\n\nPortland Police Chief Bob Day highlighted the narrow criteria for deflection eligibility, including no outstanding charges, warrants, or history of violent behavior, as well as being medically stable. If these conditions are met, officers will contact the county's deflection dispatch line to verify eligibility and connect the individual with a mobile behavioral health outreach team, which must make contact within 30 minutes. Failure to establish contact within this timeframe will result in the individual being taken into custody.\n\n***\n\nThe implementation of HB4002 marks a significant shift in Oregon's approach to drug policy, reflecting a broader debate on balancing public safety with support for those struggling with addiction. As the state navigates this new framework, the impact on individuals and local authorities will be closely watched.\n\nP.P.S I recall a trip to another country where, regardless of age, people would eat exotic dishes with their tongue fully engaged, a feat observed while shopping in bustling markets.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Oregon", "logprob": -0.10877625644207001}, {"token": "'s", "logprob": -0.3170858323574066}, {"token": " pioneering", "logprob": -0.1694791316986084}, {"token": " drug", "logprob": -0.02382541634142399}, {"token": " dec", "logprob": -1.1444026313256472e-05}, {"token": "riminal", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "ization", "logprob": -7.533743337262422e-05}, {"token": " policy", "logprob": -0.10871455818414688}, {"token": " will", "logprob": -0.6127406358718872}, {"token": " end", "logprob": -1.1324039697647095}, {"token": " on", "logprob": -1.2720932960510254}, {"token": " Sunday", "logprob": -8.391981828026474e-05}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.026103263720870018}, {"token": " replaced", "logprob": -0.6101539134979248}, {"token": " by", "logprob": -5.006777428206988e-06}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.029839398339390755}, {"token": " new", "logprob": -0.08899431675672531}, {"token": " law", "logprob": -0.00010466027742950246}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.7317061424255371}, {"token": " rec", "logprob": -0.898284912109375}, {"token": "riminal", "logprob": -3.766942609217949e-05}, {"token": "izes", "logprob": -2.6225699912174605e-05}, {"token": " possession", "logprob": -0.08203522115945816}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.2186455882765586e-06}, {"token": " small", "logprob": -6.592056161025539e-05}, {"token": " amounts", "logprob": -0.03829821199178696}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.2543604902457446e-05}, {"token": " hard", "logprob": -0.0028010678943246603}, {"token": " drugs", "logprob": -1.3828182090946939e-05}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -2.5989747047424316}, {"token": " The", "logprob": -0.9281207919120789}, {"token": " new", "logprob": 